  {
   "id": "s03",
   "text": {
    "en": "In our town, the old clock tower rings twelve times at midnight. Every single night. Except some nights, it rings thirteen times. And when you hear that thirteenth bell, there is only one rule. Go home. Lock the door. And do not open it for anyone. Not your neighbor. Not your best friend. Not even your own mother. Because whoever is knocking might not be who they look like."
