   "id": "s06",
   "text": {
    "en": "Two husbands. Same flour on their sleeves, same tired smile. Both of them swore the other one was a monster. She had until sunrise to choose. Because that's how echoes work. When the sun comes up, the echo becomes real. And the person it copied fades away, like breath on a cold window."
