  {
   "id": "s08",
   "text": {
    "en": "Back then, it happened once in a lifetime. Now the thirteenth bell rings almost every month. Everybody in town knows the drill. The second the bell rings, the streets empty. Doors slam. Shutters close. And then, in the fog, you can hear them. Walking slowly. Knocking politely. Calling out names."
